This is a classic flexbox collision issue. I can see exactly why this is breaking the layout.
When you force flex: 1 on a Stack with direction="row", it rigidly splits the width 50/50. If the text inside ("Keep Original Routing" or "Override Schedule") is slightly too long for that 50% container, it either overflows the box, pushes the custom radio button out of alignment, or wraps awkwardly.
To fix this and make it look stunning and professional—like a premium, modern SaaS card selection—we need to:
 1. **Make it responsive:** Switch the Stack to direction="column" on small screens and "row" on larger ones.
 2. **Add helper text:** A single title can look bare in a card. Adding a subtle description under the title grounds the design.
 3. **Fix the custom radio button:** We need to add minWidth to the circular Box so flexbox doesn't squish it into an oval when space gets tight.
 4. **Elevate the styles:** Add subtle box shadows, smoother transitions, and hover states.
Here are the drop-in replacements for your code.
### 1. Update the Component JSX
Replace your existing Stack block for the routing selection with this:
```jsx
<Stack 
  direction={{ xs: "column", sm: "row" }} 
  spacing={2} 
  sx={{ width: '100%', mt: 1 }}
>
  <Box 
    onClick={() => setScheduleOverrideType("KEEP")} 
    sx={jaStyles.overrideOption(scheduleOverrideType === "KEEP", false)}
  >
    <Box sx={jaStyles.overrideRadioBtn(scheduleOverrideType === "KEEP", false)} />
    <Box>
      <Typography 
        variant="subtitle2" 
        fontWeight="bold" 
        color={scheduleOverrideType === "KEEP" ? "success.dark" : "text.primary"}
      >
        Keep Original Routing
      </Typography>
      <Typography variant="caption" color="text.secondary" display="block">
        Execute as scheduled by creator
      </Typography>
    </Box>
  </Box>

  <Box 
    onClick={() => setScheduleOverrideType("OVERRIDE")} 
    sx={jaStyles.overrideOption(scheduleOverrideType === "OVERRIDE", true)}
  >
    <Box sx={jaStyles.overrideRadioBtn(scheduleOverrideType === "OVERRIDE", true)} />
    <Box>
      <Typography 
        variant="subtitle2" 
        fontWeight="bold" 
        color={scheduleOverrideType === "OVERRIDE" ? "warning.dark" : "text.primary"}
      >
        Override Schedule
      </Typography>
      <Typography variant="caption" color="text.secondary" display="block">
        Set a new execution date & time
      </Typography>
    </Box>
  </Box>
</Stack>

```
### 2. Update jaStyles
Replace your existing overrideOption and overrideRadioBtn functions in the jaStyles object with these enhanced versions:
```javascript
  // 6. Routing / Scheduling override
  overrideCardBox: { p: 2, mb: 3, backgroundColor: "#f8fafc", borderRadius: 2, borderLeft: "4px solid", borderColor: "primary.main" },
  
  overrideOption: (isActive, isOverride) => {
    const mainColor = isOverride ? "warning.main" : "success.main";
    const bgColor = isOverride ? "#fffbeb" : "#f0fdf4"; // Very light amber/green
    
    return {
      flex: 1,
      p: 2, 
      borderRadius: 3, 
      border: "2px solid", 
      borderColor: isActive ? mainColor : "#e2e8f0",
      backgroundColor: isActive ? bgColor : "#ffffff", 
      cursor: "pointer", 
      display: "flex", 
      alignItems: "flex-start", // Align to top so it looks good with 2 lines of text
      gap: 1.5, 
      transition: "all 0.2s ease-in-out",
      boxShadow: isActive 
        ? `0 4px 12px ${isOverride ? "rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.15)" : "rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.15)"}` 
        : "0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,0.05)",
      "&:hover": { 
        backgroundColor: isActive ? bgColor : "#f8fafc", 
        borderColor: isActive ? mainColor : "#cbd5e1",
        transform: "translateY(-2px)"
      }
    };
  },
  
  overrideRadioBtn: (isActive, isOverride) => {
     const mainColor = isOverride ? "warning.main" : "success.main";
     return { 
       width: 20, 
       height: 20, 
       minWidth: 20, // Prevents flexbox from squishing it into an oval
       mt: 0.25, // Micro-adjustment to align perfectly with the first line of text
       borderRadius: "50%", 
       border: isActive ? "6px solid" : "2px solid", 
       borderColor: isActive ? mainColor : "#cbd5e1", 
       backgroundColor: "white",
       transition: "all 0.2s ease-in-out"
     };
  },

```
### What this fixes structurally:
 * **The minWidth: 20** on the radio button ensures that no matter how narrow the screen gets, the circle stays perfectly round.
 * **alignItems: "flex-start"** on the card ensures that if the text wraps to a second line, the radio button stays anchored to the top rather than floating weirdly in the middle.
 * **direction={{ xs: "column", sm: "row" }}** tells MUI to stack these cards vertically on mobile devices, completely eliminating horizontal overflow, while keeping them side-by-side on desktop views.
